<title>AUSTRALIA: Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in past year.</title>
<headline>Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in past year.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a list of the 10 largest gaining and falling stocks for Australian companies included in the Australian Stock Exchange's ASX 100 index for the year to July 18.</p>
<p>Top 10 largest gains in year</p>
<p>						 Percent</p>
<p>Rank Name			 Price     change</p>
<p> 1  Oil Search		   3.80     192.31</p>
<p> 2  Sthn Pac Pete		3.75     108.33</p>
<p> 3  Howard Smith		13.80	78.76</p>
<p> 4  FLC-Building div	   3.88	73.92</p>
<p> 5  Natl Aust Bank	    19.38	68.96</p>
<p> 6  Transurban Group	1070.00	68.50</p>
<p> 7  A N Z Bank		  10.15	67.77</p>
<p> 8  Southcorp Hldgs	    4.95	65.00</p>
<p> 9  Wesfarmers		  12.01	64.52</p>
<p>10  Fletcher-Energy	    4.35	64.03</p>
<p>Top 10 largest falls in year</p>
<p>						 Percent</p>
<p>Rank Name				    Price     change</p>
<p> 1  Goldfields		   1.25     -53.70</p>
<p> 2  Acacia Resources	   1.38     -50.93</p>
<p> 3  Sons Of Gwalia	     4.75     -41.36</p>
<p> 4  Newcrest Mining	    2.70     -38.64</p>
<p> 5  Plutonic Rsc		 3.80     -32.14</p>
<p> 6  RGC			    4.19     -27.76</p>
<p> 7  Davids Limited	     1.20     -27.27</p>
<p> 8  Great Central		2.69     -22.70</p>
<p> 9  Crown			  2.08     -20.13</p>
<p>10  Normandy Min		 1.57     -15.59</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
